<title>USA: FHLMC sets $1.4 billion of REMIC securities.</title>
<headline>FHLMC sets $1.4 billion of REMIC securities.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp (Freddie Mac or FHLMC) said it issued $1.4 billion of Real Estate Mortgage Investment Conduit (REMIC) securities.</p>
<p>Strip series 180 has a coupon of 7.5 percent and is backed by 30-year single-family fixed-rate mortgages, Freddie Mac said. The issue has a weighted coupon of 8.047 percent and a weighted average maturity of 355 months, the agency said.</p>
<p>Freddie Mac said Series 180 was underwritten by the following firms:</p>
<p>Dealer					    Amount</p>
<p>Bear, Stearns &amp; Co Inc		    $ 50 million</p>
<p>Deutsche Morgan Grenfell		   100 million</p>
<p>DLJ						250 million</p>
<p>Freddie Mac SS&amp;TG			     50 million</p>
<p>CS First Boston				100 million</p>
<p>Greenwich Capital Markets Inc	    100 million</p>
<p>Goldman, Sachs &amp; Co			  100 million</p>
<p>Merrill Lynch &amp; Co Inc		     125 million</p>
<p>Nomura Securities International Inc     75 million</p>
<p>UBS Securities LLC			   250 million</p>
<p>Painewebber Inc				200 million</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1562</p>
